  "text": "```verilog\nmodule arbiter #\n(\n    parameter PORTS = 4,\n    parameter ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN = 0,\n    parameter ARB_BLOCK = 0,\n    parameter ARB_BLOCK_ACK = 1,\n    parameter ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY = 0\n)\n(\n    input  wire                     clk,\n    input  wire                     rst,\n    input  wire [PORTS-1:0]         request,\n    input  wire [PORTS-1:0]         acknowledge,\n    output wire [PORTS-1:0]         grant,\n    output wire                     grant_valid,\n    output wire [$clog2(PORTS)-1:0] grant_encoded\n);\n\n    localparam NUM_PORTS = PORTS;\n    localparam ENC_WIDTH = $clog2(PORTS);\n\n    reg [NUM_PORTS-1:0] grant_reg;\n    reg [ENC_WIDTH-1:0] grant_enc_reg;\n    reg                 grant_valid_reg;\n\n    // For round-robin, track the last granted port to rotate priority\n    reg [ENC_WIDTH-1:0] last_grant_reg;\n\n    // Internal signals\n    wire [NUM_PORTS-1:0] priority_mask;\n    wire [NUM_PORTS-1:0] masked_request;\n    wire [NUM_PORTS-1:0] unmasked_request;\n    wire [NUM_PORTS-1:0] candidate;\n    wire [NUM_PORTS-1:0] grant_next;\n    wire [ENC_WIDTH-1:0] grant_enc_next;\n    wire                 grant_valid_next;\n\n    // Generate priority mask for round-robin\n    // If ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN is set, we rotate priority based on last_grant_reg\n    // The mask should have 1s for ports with higher priority than the last granted port\n    // For LSB high priority: lower index = higher priority\n    // For MSB high priority: higher index = higher priority\n\n    // Let's define the priority order\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY is 1, port 0 has highest priority, port NUM_PORTS-1 has lowest\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY is 0, port NUM_PORTS-1 has highest priority, port 0 has lowest\n\n    // For round-robin, we want to give priority to ports after the last granted port\n    // in the priority order.\n\n    // Let's create a function to determine the priority order\n    // Actually, let's think about this differently.\n\n    // For fixed priority:\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: grant the lowest index request\n    // If !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: grant the highest index request\n\n    // For round-robin:\n    // We rotate the priority so that the port after the last granted port (in priority order) gets highest priority.\n\n    // Let's define a helper to get the \"next\" port in priority order after a given port\n    // Priority order:\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: 0, 1, 2, ..., NUM_PORTS-1\n    // If !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: NUM_PORTS-1, NUM_PORTS-2, ..., 0\n\n    // For round-robin, we want to start searching from the port after last_grant in the priority order.\n\n    // Let's create a mask that indicates which ports are \"after\" last_grant in the priority order.\n    // Ports in the mask will be considered first.\n\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   Priority order: 0 (highest), 1, 2, ..., NUM_PORTS-1 (lowest)\n    //   After last_grant = L, the next in priority order is L+1, L+2, ..., NUM_PORTS-1, 0, 1, ..., L-1\n    //   So the mask should have 1s for ports > L (in index), and then wrap around to 0..L-1\n    //   Actually, for round-robin, we want to give priority to ports that come after L in the cyclic priority order.\n    //   So if L=2, the order is 3, 0, 1, 2 (if LSB high priority, priority is 0>1>2>3, so after 2 is 3, then wrap to 0,1,2)\n    //   Wait, I need to be careful.\n\n    // Let me reconsider. In round-robin arbitration, the idea is that after granting to port L, the next grant should go to the next port in the cyclic order.\n    // The cyclic order depends on the priority direction.\n\n    // If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   Natural priority: 0 > 1 > 2 > ... > NUM_PORTS-1\n    //   Cyclic order after L: (L+1) % NUM_PORTS, (L+2) % NUM_PORTS, ..., L\n    //   So we want to search in this order.\n\n    // If !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   Natural priority: NUM_PORTS-1 > NUM_PORTS-2 > ... > 0\n    //   Cyclic order after L: (L-1+NUM_PORTS) % NUM_PORTS, (L-2+NUM_PORTS) % NUM_PORTS, ..., L\n    //   So we want to search in this order.\n\n    // To implement this, we can create a mask that has 1s for the ports that should be considered first (i.e., those after L in the cyclic order).\n\n    // For ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   Ports after L: L+1, L+2, ..., NUM_PORTS-1, 0, 1, ..., L-1\n    //   Mask: bits [NUM_PORTS-1:L+1] = 1, bits [L-1:0] = 1, bit L = 0\n    //   Actually, we want to search in the order L+1, L+2, ..., NUM_PORTS-1, 0, 1, ..., L-1\n    //   So the mask for the \"first half\" is bits [NUM_PORTS-1:L+1] set to 1\n    //   And the \"second half\" is bits [L-1:0] set to 1\n\n    // For !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   Ports after L: L-1, L-2, ..., 0, NUM_PORTS-1, NUM_PORTS-2, ..., L+1\n    //   Mask: bits [L-1:0] = 1, bits [NUM_PORTS-1:L+1] = 1\n\n    // Let's create the mask\n    reg [NUM_PORTS-1:0] rr_mask;\n\n    always @(*) begin\n        if (ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN) begin\n            if (ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY) begin\n                // Priority order: 0 > 1 > 2 > ... > NUM_PORTS-1\n                // After last_grant, search: last_grant+1, ..., NUM_PORTS-1, 0, ..., last_grant-1\n                rr_mask = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                for (integer i = 0; i < NUM_PORTS; i = i + 1) begin\n                    if (i > last_grant_reg) begin\n                        rr_mask[i] = 1'b1;\n                    end\n                end\n            end else begin\n                // Priority order: NUM_PORTS-1 > NUM_PORTS-2 > ... > 0\n                // After last_grant, search: last_grant-1, ..., 0, NUM_PORTS-1, ..., last_grant+1\n                rr_mask = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                for (integer i = 0; i < NUM_PORTS; i = i + 1) begin\n                    if (i < last_grant_reg) begin\n                        rr_mask[i] = 1'b1;\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end else begin\n            rr_mask = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Now, for the actual arbitration:\n    // If ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN:\n    //   First, check if any request is in rr_mask. If so, grant the highest priority one among them.\n    //   If no request in rr_mask, grant the highest priority one among all requests.\n    // If !ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN:\n    //   Grant the highest priority one among all requests.\n\n    // \"Highest priority\" depends on ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY:\n    //   If ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: lowest index wins\n    //   If !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: highest index wins\n\n    // Let's create a function to find the highest priority request in a given set of requests\n\n    // For ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: find the lowest index with request=1\n    // For !ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY: find the highest index with request=1\n\n    // Let's create two versions of the request set:\n    //   masked_request: requests that are in rr_mask (for round-robin first pass)\n    //   unmasked_request: all requests (for round-robin second pass or fixed priority)\n\n    assign masked_request = request & rr_mask;\n    assign unmasked_request = request;\n\n    // Function to find the grant for a given request vector\n    // Returns the grant vector and encoded value\n\n    // Let's use a combinational block to determine the grant\n\n    reg [NUM_PORTS-1:0] grant_comb;\n    reg [ENC_WIDTH-1:0] grant_enc_comb;\n    reg                 grant_valid_comb;\n\n    always @(*) begin\n        grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n        grant_enc_comb = {ENC_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n        grant_valid_comb = 1'b0;\n\n        if (ARB_TYPE_ROUND_ROBIN) begin\n            // First, try to grant from masked_request\n            if (masked_request != 0) begin\n                if (ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY) begin\n                    // Find lowest index with request=1 in masked_request\n                    for (integer i = 0; i < NUM_PORTS; i = i + 1) begin\n                        if (masked_request[i]) begin\n                            grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                            grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                            grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                            grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                            i = NUM_PORTS; // Break out of loop\n                        end\n                    end\n                end else begin\n                    // Find highest index with request=1 in masked_request\n                    for (integer i = NUM_PORTS-1; i >= 0; i = i - 1) begin\n                        if (masked_request[i]) begin\n                            grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                            grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                            grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                            grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                            i = -1; // Break out of loop\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n            end else begin\n                // No request in masked_request, try unmasked_request\n                if (unmasked_request != 0) begin\n                    if (ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY) begin\n                        for (integer i = 0; i < NUM_PORTS; i = i + 1) begin\n                            if (unmasked_request[i]) begin\n                                grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                                grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                                grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                                grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                                i = NUM_PORTS;\n                            end\n                        end\n                    end else begin\n                        for (integer i = NUM_PORTS-1; i >= 0; i = i - 1) begin\n                            if (unmasked_request[i]) begin\n                                grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                                grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                                grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                                grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                                i = -1;\n                            end\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end else begin\n            // Fixed priority\n            if (unmasked_request != 0) begin\n                if (ARB_LSB_HIGH_PRIORITY) begin\n                    for (integer i = 0; i < NUM_PORTS; i = i + 1) begin\n                        if (unmasked_request[i]) begin\n                            grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                            grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                            grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                            grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                            i = NUM_PORTS;\n                        end\n                    end\n                end else begin\n                    for (integer i = NUM_PORTS-1; i >= 0; i = i - 1) begin\n                        if (unmasked_request[i]) begin\n                            grant_comb = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n                            grant_comb[i] = 1'b1;\n                            grant_enc_comb = i[ENC_WIDTH-1:0];\n                            grant_valid_comb = 1'b1;\n                            i = -1;\n                        end\n                    end\n                end\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Now handle the blocking behavior\n    // If ARB_BLOCK is set:\n    //   If ARB_BLOCK_ACK is nonzero: hold grant until acknowledge is received\n    //   If ARB_BLOCK_ACK is zero: hold grant until request drops\n\n    // We need to track the current grant state\n\n    // Let's define the next state logic\n\n    always @(*) begin\n        if (rst) begin\n            grant_next = {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n            grant_enc_next = {ENC_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            grant_valid_next = 1'b0;\n        end else if (ARB_BLOCK) begin\n            if (grant_valid_reg) begin\n                // Currently granting\n                if (ARB_BLOCK_ACK) begin\n                    // Hold until acknowledge\n                    if (acknowledge & grant_reg) begin\n                        // Acknowledge received, can change grant\n                        grant_next = grant_comb;\n                        grant_enc_next = grant_enc_comb;\n                        grant_valid_next = grant_valid_comb;\n                    end else begin\n                        // Hold current grant\n                        grant_next = grant_reg;\n                        grant_enc_next = grant_enc_reg;\n                        grant_valid_next = 1'b1;\n                    end\n                end else begin\n                    // Hold until request drops\n                    if (request & grant_reg) begin\n                        // Request still present, hold\n                        grant_next = grant_reg;\n                        grant_enc_next = grant_enc_reg;\n                        grant_valid_next = 1'b1;\n                    end else begin\n                        // Request dropped, can change grant\n                        grant_next = grant_comb;\n                        grant_enc_next = grant_enc_comb;\n                        grant_valid_next = grant_valid_comb;\n                    end\n                end\n            end else begin\n                // Not currently granting, take new grant\n                grant_next = grant_comb;\n                grant_enc_next = grant_enc_comb;\n                grant_valid_next = grant_valid_comb;\n            end\n        end else begin\n            // No blocking, always update\n            grant_next = grant_comb;\n            grant_enc_next = grant_enc_comb;\n            grant_valid_next = grant_valid_comb;\n        end\n    end\n\n    // Sequential logic\n    always @(posedge clk) begin\n        if (rst) begin\n            grant_reg <= {NUM_PORTS{1'b0}};\n            grant_enc_reg <= {ENC_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n            grant_valid_reg <= 1'b0;\n            last_grant_reg <= {ENC_WIDTH{1'b0}};\n        end else begin\n            grant_reg <= grant_next;\n            grant_enc_reg <= grant_enc_next;\n            grant_valid_reg <= grant_valid_next;\n\n            // Update last_grant_reg for round-robin\n            if (grant_valid_next) begin\n                last_grant_reg <= grant_enc_next;\n            end\n        end\n    end\n\n    assign grant = grant_reg;\n    assign grant_valid = grant_valid_reg;\n    assign grant_encoded = grant_enc_reg;\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
